# Authoritative context service: bounded integration and full-scope preparation

The bounded service passes on both existing historical development repositories.
It uses actual native snapshot/scanner, semantic bundle, capsule assessment,
Datasets context-pack authority, Accelerator consumer, and Kit immutable storage
under one pinned normal-import profile. Independent consumer processes materialize
all 302 regular files (11,781,935 bytes), retaining one documentation symlink as
opaque metadata. No source is substituted, and no model call or repair scorer runs.

| Existing development repository | Python files analyzed / public Python files | Native symbols / edges | Unknown edge occurrences | Dependency capsules | Initial snapshot + scan + bundle seconds |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| xmltodict | 1 / 6 | 29 / 408 | 384 | 0 | 6.585 |
| pyparsing | 5 / 154 | 114 / 996 | 971 | 4 | 18.694 |

This table is the explicitly bounded semantic scope in
`results_v6_bounded_index/semantic_scope.json` (per case). Every remaining source
file is retained; the 5 and 149 unparsed Python paths are named missing evidence.
Two pyparsing capsules receive native exact admission and two receive conservative
admission. These are descriptive/freshness classifications and do not establish
behavioral correctness or grant source omission. The locally authored acceptance
obligation remains unexecuted. Raw binary assets also remain retained.

The controller and producer/consumer source files are frozen by SHA-256 before
execution. The public archive/tree bytes and modes bind a newly computed Git tree;
the upstream commit's full Git object provenance was not freshly authenticated.
The runtime pins complete ASEH Accelerator/Kit plus an isolated Datasets source
variant containing one native verifier optimization. Unchanged package files use
hardlinks; the changed file is a separate inode and the original source is unchanged.

The independent audit verifies exact source custody and executes four unique raw
source expansion commands. All four match frozen bytes; two outside-scope requests
fail. The producers separately execute six native source materializations (some
capsules share a file). Across the two consumers, 22 negative controls reject
identity/payload/byte/current-root misuse. Four unchanged/target-comment transitions
have identical cold/incremental state CIDs, semantic root CIDs, and reachable blocks.
Producer wall time including those extra identity controls is 33.17 and 99.18 seconds;
those figures must not be compared with the initial-preparation column above.

Native compatibility flags remain insufficient execution authority: these packs
report `sufficient` and `expansion_required=false` despite named missing evidence.
Its fixed token costs are not tokenizer measurements. Native exact freshness also
omits the required-source CID mapping; the evaluation caller separately compares
that mapping, resolves every source bundle/member, and verifies current bytes.
Unsigned candidate bytes never become a published current root or signed receipt.

Full-scope preparation is separately measured. Unmodified xmltodict preparation
takes 64.838 seconds excluding imports, with 162 symbols, 1,487 edges and 1,281 unknown
edges. Unmodified pyparsing completes scanning in 145.51 seconds (3,957 symbols,
55,859 edges) but does not finish semantic bundle preparation within the 600-second
producer bound. This timeout remains in `results_v5/outcome.json`.

Profiling identifies repeated node-CID set construction inside every link iteration
of native `verify_symbol_merkle_dag`. The isolated patch moves that immutable local
membership index outside the loop. It retains all block/CID/record/layering/membership
checks and all source admission code. The 44 original native Merkle, source, and
freshness tests pass. Full xmltodict preparation becomes 26.296 seconds, with exactly
the same native state and semantic root and the same unknown edges. These are single
local timing observations; ContextPack toolchain identities intentionally differ
between source profiles. `comparison_v5_v7_xml.json` binds the exact paired
measurements and equal roots/source bundles. The hoist-only full pyparsing run also
times out: scan 145.615 seconds, whole producer 600.197 seconds. This second censored
result is separate in `results_v7_full_index/outcome.json`; the index improvement
does not yet qualify full pyparsing preparation.

`service_contract_v6.json` provides the controller integration contract. The current
qualified endpoint materializes these frozen source cases; arbitrary candidate edits,
dynamic objective/source rebinding, model context budgeting, signed trust, routing,
procedure execution, and full multi-step workload outcomes remain to be integrated.
The broader study protocol remains `../../next_stage_protocol.md`. This increment
establishes neither whole-system token savings nor fresh held-out efficacy.

For controller integration, `routing_enrollment_v1` separately enrolls all four
existing constructed routing tasks. Only source, objective and visible validation
are projected into native producer authority. Four real producer/consumer roundtrips
pass, and `context_read_v1.py` repeatedly returns the exact source/objective/visible
validation after native pack verification and source expansion. The independent
`routing_context_audit_v1.json` verifies all four reads, rejects controller source
and objective mismatches and an actual current source-file mutation, then verifies
the exact restored source again. The controller must consume these returned inputs
to claim integration; this enrollment alone has no routing or model outcome.
